[30.048378, "o", " │ The RECORD file will tell us what files should be present. Let me reinsta…\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ `ensurepip` thinks it's already installed so it won't reinstall. Let me f…\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info && python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info &&…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify it works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me do a quick functional test to confirm package installation works:\r\n[approval] bash: p"]
[30.048383, "o", "ip3 install --user --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --user --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\nEverything is working now.\r\n\r\n**Diagnosis:** The `pip` Python package was missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` — only the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory remained. The actual `pip/` package directory had been deleted or corrupted, so the `pip3` script (which lives in `/usr/local/bin/`) couldn't import the `pip` module.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which reinstalled the full pip package from the bundled wheel. Both `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` are now functional.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=9 surface=b939125f62be\r\n"]
